{"id":95,"date":"2026-07-09T14:25:53","date_gmt":"2026-07-09T14:25:53","guid":{"rendered":"http:\/\/localhost:8181\/a-pre-winter-tune-up-checklist-built-for-altoona-weather\/"},"modified":"2026-07-14T19:43:53","modified_gmt":"2026-07-14T19:43:53","slug":"a-pre-winter-tune-up-checklist-built-for-altoona-weather","status":"publish","type":"page","link":"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/a-pre-winter-tune-up-checklist-built-for-altoona-weather\/","title":{"rendered":"A Clean Blue Flame Still Hides Bad Numbers in Altoona"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<div class=\"wp-block-group alignfull s-band s-band--dark-gradient has-contrast-background-color has-background has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-08713647 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:6rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:6rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-cover alignfull s-hero-cover\" style=\"padding-top:3rem;padding-right:2rem;padding-bottom:3rem;padding-left:2rem\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-cover__background has-contrast-background-color has-background-dim-70 has-background-dim\"><\/span><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"1024\" class=\"wp-block-cover__image-background wp-image-1757\" alt=\"furnace - professional HVAC service photo\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-furnace-1.png\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-furnace-1.png 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-furnace-1-300x300.png 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-furnace-1-150x150.png 150w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-furnace-1-768x768.png 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><div class=\"wp-block-cover__inner-container has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-cover-is-layout-ff0c90b8 wp-block-cover-is-layout-constrained\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-element-heading has-text-align-center has-base-color has-text-color s-hero-cover__title wp-block-heading\">Furnace flames lie. Numbers don&#039;t.<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-text-align-center s-lead has-base-color has-text-color has-medium-font-size wp-block-paragraph\">A furnace can pass every visual inspection and still be burning wrong, and the only place that truth shows up is in the flue gases.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons is-content-justification-center is-layout-flex wp-container-core-buttons-is-layout-35f06ea7 wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"\/contact\/\">Book Winter Readiness<\/a><\/div>\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-button is-style-outline is-style-outline--1\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"#content\">Learn More<\/a><\/div>\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div><\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"s-trust-bar\"><div class=\"s-trust__item\">15+ Years Serving PA<\/div><div class=\"s-trust__item\">Licensed &amp; Insured<\/div><div class=\"s-trust__item\">Same-Day Emergency<\/div><div class=\"s-trust__item\">Local to Your Area<\/div><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group s-diagnostic has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-b267b866 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:3rem;padding-right:3rem;padding-bottom:3rem;padding-left:3rem\">\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">\u26a0\ufe0f Six silent furnace failures your eyes will never catch<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Cracked heat exchanger venting combustion gas into the basement air stream<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Carbon monoxide production rising undetected because flame color stays blue<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Weak draft from a deteriorating coal-era chimney, spilling gases indoors<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Efficiency loss creeping up five percent per year \u2014 invisible until the bill arrives<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Condensate trap silting closed, weeks away from a midwinter shutdown<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Flame signal dropping below spec, lockout scheduled for the coldest night<\/li>\n\n<\/ul>\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group alignfull s-band s-band--sand has-tint-background-color has-background has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-08713647 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:6rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:6rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Why visual inspection fails in a six-month heating season<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group s-indent has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\">\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Altoona heats longer and harder than most of Pennsylvania. The city sits roughly twelve hundred feet up, wedged between Brush Mountain and the Allegheny Front, and the valley holds its cold \u2014 furnaces here routinely fire from early October into April. A machine asked to run six months out of twelve deserves more than a vacuuming and a thumbs-up before the season opens.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Yet most of what gets sold as a tune-up is exactly that: pull the doors, brush the burners, eyeball the flame, gone in twenty minutes. Combustion problems do not announce themselves to eyeballs.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">They announce themselves as numbers \u2014 oxygen percentage, carbon monoxide concentration, stack temperature, draft pressure \u2014 and a technician who never puts an analyzer probe into your flue has not actually tested whether your furnace is burning safely or wastefully.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group s-quote s-quote--dramatic has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-pullquote\"><blockquote><p>A clean blue flame is the most dangerous thing in HVAC: it looks right while burning wrong.<\/p><cite>Combustion analysis, the measured way<\/cite><\/blockquote><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-media-text has-media-on-the-right\" style=\"grid-template-columns:auto 50%\"><div class=\"wp-block-media-text__content\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Four flue readings and what they reveal<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Natural gas burns blue, and a tidy blue flame looks reassuring. But flame color is a crude signal. Proper combustion is a ratio problem \u2014 a specific gas input meeting a specific volume of air \u2014 and either side of that ratio can drift without changing how the fire looks. Dust chokes the burner intakes, gas pressure creeps as a regulator ages, flue restriction slows the exhaust.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The flame stays blue long after the chemistry has gone off. The byproduct that matters most is carbon monoxide, produced whenever the fire runs short of oxygen. It is invisible and odorless, and at the concentrations where a technician should intervene, it changes nothing you can see or smell at the burner. The only honest way to know is to sample the flue and read the number.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Oxygen: 6\u20139% healthy; lower runs rich (CO risk), higher wastes heat up the chimney<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Carbon monoxide: under 100 ppm stable; rising CO when blower starts signals heat exchanger crack<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Stack temperature: 350\u2013450\u00b0F for standard furnace; ~110\u00b0F for condensing \u2014 tells you whether the exchanger is working<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Draft pressure: measured in hundredths of an inch water column \u2014 confirms chimney or vent is actually pulling<\/li>\n\n<\/ul>\n\n<\/div><figure class=\"wp-block-media-text__media\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"1024\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-1.png\" alt=\"technician - professional HVAC service photo\" class=\"wp-image-1755\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-1.png 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-1-300x300.png 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-1-150x150.png 150w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-1-768x768.png 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><span class=\"s-img-badge s-img-badge--ai\" title=\"AI-generated (gemini-2.5-flash-image)\">AI<\/span><\/figure><\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group alignfull s-band s-band--warm-gradient has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-08713647 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:6rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:6rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">What the measured tune-up catches before winter does<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list s-steps\">\n<li>Combustion analysis \u2014 Flue gas sampling at steady fire and at ignition, logged in writing. This is where the invisible failures surface.<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Heat exchanger inspection \u2014 Video scope inside the exchanger; look for cracks or deterioration that would spill gas into living space.<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Airflow and temperature rise \u2014 Measure supply-to-return air temp differential against nameplate spec. Starved airflow predicts exchanger cracking years early.<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Electrical diagnostics \u2014 Flame signal in microamps, ignitor resistance in ohms. These numbers predict lockouts weeks before they happen.<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Condensate system (90+ furnaces) \u2014 Trap pulled, flushed, and drained. A plugged trap causes more midwinter shutdowns than combustion issues.<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Flue and chimney check \u2014 Draft measurement, chimney liner condition assessment, orphaned water heater detection. In Altoona&#039;s coal-conversion homes, this is critical.<\/li>\n\n<\/ul>\n\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-media-text\" style=\"grid-template-columns:50% auto\"><figure class=\"wp-block-media-text__media\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"1024\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-furnace-2.png\" alt=\"furnace - professional HVAC service photo\" class=\"wp-image-1758\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-furnace-2.png 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-furnace-2-300x300.png 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-furnace-2-150x150.png 150w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-furnace-2-768x768.png 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><span class=\"s-img-badge s-img-badge--ai\" title=\"AI-generated (gemini-2.5-flash-image)\">AI<\/span><\/figure><div class=\"wp-block-media-text__content\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Altoona&#039;s railroad-era chimneys: what they need now<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">A large share of Altoona&#039;s housing went up for Pennsylvania Railroad families between the 1880s and the 1920s \u2014 the two-story frame houses that fill Juniata, Fairview, and Llyswen \u2014 and those homes carry masonry chimneys built for coal.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here is the pattern we watch for: the furnace gets upgraded to a sidewall-vented condensing model, and the gas water heater is left behind as the only appliance on a chimney sized for two. Venting pros call it an orphaned water heater.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The oversized flue lets exhaust cool and condense inside the masonry, the liner deteriorates, draft weakens, and the risk of spilling combustion gases into the basement grows each season. A thorough visit checks the water heater&#039;s draft and the chimney&#039;s condition, not just the furnace&#039;s.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The other local fact is arithmetic: Blair County&#039;s heating season runs weeks longer on both ends than southeastern Pennsylvania&#039;s, so a furnace here logs far more firing hours per calendar year \u2014 and wear parts age on hours, not birthdays. That is also why October appointments are calm; November gets triage.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Coal-conversion homes: original chimneys unlined; direct-vent replacement or relining needed<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Dual-fuel setups: electric to 25\u00b0F, gas backup below \u2014 optimal for Altoona&#039;s climate profile<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Blair County: 6,500 heating degree days \u2014 furnaces run 25% longer than state average<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Horseshoe Curve corridor: wind channeling increases infiltration in exposed hilltop homes<\/li>\n\n<\/ul>\n\n<\/div><\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group alignfull s-band s-band--cream has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-08713647 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:6rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:6rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list s-pills s-pills--glass\">\n<li>6,500 heating degree days annually<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Coal-era chimneys throughout the city<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Furnaces log 25% more hours than statewide average<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Orphaned water heaters create venting risks<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Condensate traps fail predictably in October\u2013November<\/li>\n\n<\/ul>\n\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-element-heading has-text-align-center wp-block-heading\">Who needs this visit most in Altoona<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns alignwide s-cards-3 is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-794e3cfa wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column s-card is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Original frame homes<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Masonry chimneys from the coal era, relined or converted to gas. Flue safety and draft testing are non-negotiable.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column s-card is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Furnace replaced, water heater kept<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The orphaned-heater pattern. If the old chimney now serves only the water heater, venting risk grows yearly.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column s-card is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Furnace past ten seasons<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">In Altoona&#039;s climate, ten years of runtime equals twelve to fifteen in milder zones. Wear parts are aging fast.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-element-heading has-text-align-center wp-block-heading\">Tune-up questions Altoona homeowners ask<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group s-accordion s-accordion--bordered has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-1583283a wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\">\n<details class=\"wp-block-details is-layout-flow wp-block-details-is-layout-flow\"><summary>When should I book, and does timing really matter?<\/summary>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">September through mid-October is the window. The furnace can be test-fired and corrected before you depend on it nightly, parts that measure marginal can be ordered without urgency, and you are ahead of the first-cold-snap rush that compresses everyone&#039;s schedule once the valley turns cold.<\/p>\n\n<\/details>\n\n\n\n<details class=\"wp-block-details is-layout-flow wp-block-details-is-layout-flow\"><summary>My furnace is only a few years old. Is this necessary?<\/summary>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Yes, for two reasons. Condensing furnaces have a drainage system that clogs regardless of age, and most manufacturer warranties expect documented annual maintenance. A young furnace also deserves a baseline: readings recorded now make drift obvious in year six instead of mysterious in year twelve.<\/p>\n\n<\/details>\n\n\n\n<details class=\"wp-block-details is-layout-flow wp-block-details-is-layout-flow\"><summary>I have CO alarms. Doesn&#039;t that cover the safety side?<\/summary>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Alarms are the last line, not the first. Consumer CO alarms are designed to tolerate low concentrations for hours before sounding, because they exist to prevent acute poisoning \u2014 not to flag a furnace drifting out of tune. An analyzer reads the problem at its source, at levels an alarm will never mention. Keep the alarms; add the measurement.<\/p>\n\n<\/details>\n\n\n\n<details class=\"wp-block-details is-layout-flow wp-block-details-is-layout-flow\"><summary>What does this cost, and what am I getting?<\/summary>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">A full combustion tune-up visit takes roughly an hour and ends with your furnace&#039;s readings in writing \u2014 oxygen, CO, stack temperature, draft, flame signal, temperature rise, electrical readings \u2014 plus a baseline to compare against next fall. You are getting knowledge, not just a service. A furnace that measures healthy is worth paying to know about.<\/p>\n\n<\/details>\n\n\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group alignfull s-band s-band--dark-gradient has-contrast-background-color has-background has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-08713647 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:6rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:6rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group s-cta has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\">\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Put this winter&#039;s numbers on the record<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Book your measured combustion tune-up while October still has dates open. You will get a baseline to protect against silent failures and a printout to compare against next year.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons is-content-justification-center is-layout-flex wp-container-core-buttons-is-layout-35f06ea7 wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"\/contact\/\">Reserve the Combustion Test<\/a><\/div>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-element-heading has-text-align-center wp-block-heading\">Our Work in Your Neighborhood<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-gallery alignwide has-nested-images columns-3 is-cropped s-gallery wp-block-gallery-2 is-layout-flex wp-block-gallery-is-layout-flex\">\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"1024\" data-id=\"1756\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-2.png\" alt=\"technician - professional HVAC service photo\" class=\"wp-image-1756\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-2.png 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-2-300x300.png 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-2-150x150.png 150w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-2-768x768.png 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><span class=\"s-img-badge s-img-badge--ai\" title=\"AI-generated (gemini-2.5-flash-image)\">AI<\/span><\/figure>\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"768\" data-id=\"19